    "verdict_label": "RECALL RISK",
    "verdict_summary": "Candidate generation successfully partitions scenarios and eliminates 75.25% of global theoretical pairs, operating with high throughput (63.13s) and low memory (326 MB). However, empirical evaluation against ground truth reveals a critical recall vulnerability: on overlapping-field-of-view camera intersections, vehicles visible simultaneously across cameras (delta_t < 0) or crossing adjacent FOV boundaries in <0.5s suffer a 64.61% false negative rejection rate (182 negative-time rejections, 17 excessive-speed rejections). Simultaneously, unbounded temporal windows allow 3.29M candidate pairs with delta_t > 120s to survive with zero recall benefit."
